{"credentialModelOpt.get() is called without first checking credentialModelOpt.isPresent(), which throws NoSuchElementException if no recovery-code credential exists for the user instead of a user-friendly failure": 0.9288543462753296, "Provider ID is hardcoded as \"keycloak-recovery-authn-codes\" instead of using RecoveryAuthnCodesCredentialProviderFactory.PROVIDER_ID constant, risking silent mismatch if the ID changes": 0.4686531126499176, "generatedCodes contains raw (unhashed) recovery codes that are serialized and stored via UserCredentialModel.getChallengeResponse() in user storage, while the local DB path correctly stores hashed codes - this is a security vulnerability as attackers with read access to user storage would obtain usable codes": 0.8930215835571289, "When updateCredential succeeds via user storage path, the used-code tracking that normally happens in RecoveryAuthnCodesCredentialProvider.isValid() does not occur - BackwardsCompatibilityUserStorage.isValid() checks if code exists without removing it, allowing the same recovery code to be used multiple times for federated-storage users": 0.8968883156776428, "List generatedKeys is a raw type instead of List<String>, suppressing compile-time type safety and producing unchecked cast warnings": 0.20454448461532593, "Typo in config alias: \"delayed-suthenticator-config\" should be \"delayed-authenticator-config\", which could cause subtle test failures if the alias is looked up elsewhere": 0.11534515768289566}